group: D6h
formula: C6H6
construction: its two sets of equivalent atoms
headline: 
source: MO levels: RHF, def2-SVP · 
note: Model from extended Hückel (qualitative) · model energies in eV · calculation in Hartree · electrons: C6 6, drawn 6; H6 0, drawn 0; model and calculation: 6 drawn + 0 folded (0 levels) = 6 · labels in D<sub>6h</sub>
about: The extended Hückel diagram explains the calculation's orbitals: nothing more, nothing less.\n\n**The model.** Every column is extended Hückel (Alvarez parameters). The middle column is the molecule's own extended Hückel run, the side columns are the two fragments' (C6 and H6). The basis is the same in all three, so the lines are an exact projection of each model MO on the fragment orbitals: a line joins a model MO to a fragment level that makes up at least 10 % of it.\n\n**Bonding and antibonding** are read from the sign of each model MO's overlap population between the two fragments, then paired per symmetry label and degeneracy, so each antibonding level has its bonding partner; a level without a partner is non-bonding. Colours mark the pairs.\n\n**The calculation** is the column on the right, on its own energy axis in Hartree and to scale. For each model level it shows the calculated orbital (or set of near-degenerate orbitals) with the largest overlap with it, at its calculated energy, in the colour of the model level it matches. A level marked ≈ matches only loosely (overlap below 0.80; the value is in the hover text). Labels are those of the matched calculated orbital. Clicking a level shows that orbital in 3-D.\n\nThe model explains your occupied orbitals and the LUMO in the right order. Virtual orbitals above the LUMO depend strongly on the basis set.\n\n**Total electrons: 6** (C6 6, H6 0).\n\nEach model level carries a short grey tag naming the fragment orbitals it is mostly made of (shares of at least 20 %), such as Cr d or CO π*. Ligand-field view hides empty ligand-centred levels such as CO π*; transitions into them are charge transfer, not d–d.\n\nDrawn as its two sets of equivalent atoms. This molecule has no central atom, so there is no central-atom diagram; combining fragments of it instead needs a subgroup and a choice.\n\n**Orbital labels.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D6h; the code reported none.
verdict: ok The model explains your occupied orbitals and the LUMO in the right order.
